  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f867e729cd163844296773769e23f97f, type: 3}
  m_Name: NeedleJack
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Rarety: 2
  m_Description: "He moves through the shadows like smoke, leaving only whispers
    and corpses behind. Known on the streets as \"Needle\", he is both assassin and
    alchemist, a junkie with a taste for his own venom. Where others fear poison,
    he craves it \u2014 mixing deadly concoctions in the flickering light of filthy
    back-alley labs, testing each new formula first on himself. His veins carry more
    toxins than blood; every dose a gamble between enlightenment and oblivion. The
    scars on his arms aren\u2019t just from the syringes \u2014 they\u2019re maps
    of where death kissed him and walked away disappointed.\\n\\nNeedle\u2019s eyes
    burn with the hollow intensity of someone who has seen too much and cares too
    little. His grin is cracked and crooked, a side effect of too many near-death
    highs. Despite the chaos of his addiction, his hands never shake. Each blade
    he carries is laced with poisons of his own design \u2014 hallucinogens, paralytics,
    slow burners that make the kill last hours if he\u2019s feeling particularly
    cruel.\\n\\nHe doesn't take contracts for the money. He takes them for the thrill,
    the art, the chemical experiments. Killing is just another part of his process,
    another ingredient in his endless search for the perfect high. Rumors say he
    once dosed an entire crime syndicate with vaporized fear toxin, then sat cross-legged
    among their twitching bodies, watching their nightmares play out like theater.\\n\\nHe's
    thin, wiry, with a frame more shadow than flesh, wrapped in tattered leathers
    stained with who-knows-what. Pouches and vials clink softly at his belt, each
    one a secret, each one a sin. His scent is a cocktail of coppery blood, sour
    sweat, and sweet chemical rot. But beneath the madness, there\u2019s a mind as
    sharp as his needles \u2014 calculating, patient, and endlessly inventive.\\n\\nEvery
    job is a test. Every kill, an experiment. And if the poison doesn\u2019t drop
    his target fast enough\u2026 well, he\u2019ll just slip a little under his own
    tongue and see what happens next."
  m_DescriptionVariables: []
